IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rawq-dates`

-- Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland) -- s 2, commencement, and what the deposited
-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 shows of it.
--
-- s 2 as passed fixes two days and one moving point:
--   s 2(1): 1 December 2024 for part 2's heading, ss 3, 28(1), 31, 37, 38 and 46 to 48, s 51 so far as it inserts
--           chapter 11 part 10's heading and ss 282 and 285, s 52(2) so far as it inserts the definitions "class
--           member" and "registered employee organisation", and s 52(3);
--   s 2(2): 1 July 2025 for the provisions of part 2 not in force on 30 June 2025, part 3, ss 56 to 59, part 6 and
--           schedule 1;
--   s 2(3): part 11 and schedule 2 immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences
--           (that day is not in the deposited sources).
-- Provisions s 2 does not name (ss 1, 2, part 4's heading, ss 55 and 59A, parts 5, 6A, 7, 8, 9, 9A and 10) are left to
-- the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited (fork F2).
--
-- s 47A sits between ss 47 and 48, and is read as within "sections ... 46 to 48" in s 2(1)(b) (fork F1). The deposited
-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (the version in force from 19 May 2025, current on 6 November 2026) agrees: it shows
-- new ss 204 and 205 in force and, in s 285AA (inserted by later legislation), speaks of them "as in force from
-- 1 December 2024".
--
-- The 1 July 2025 group did not, on the deposited evidence, commence on that day: none of it is in the Anti-
-- Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026, and that Act's s 285AA ties the new burden of proof to "the
-- commencement of section 7B of the amendment Act", a day it does not give. Later legislation, not deposited here,
-- has deferred or changed that commencement (finding 1). The claimant's questions therefore ask whether, and on what
-- day, the 1 July 2025 group has commenced, rather than assume 1 July 2025.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024: commencement`

-- The amending Act's provisions, grouped as s 2 groups them and as a complainant meets them. "the Act" in the glosses is
-- the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991, which part 2 and schedule 1 amend (s 3).
DECLARE `Provision of the amending Act` IS ONE OF
    `ss 1 and 2 (short title and commencement)`
    `part 2 heading and s 3 (Act amended)`
    `s 28(1) (note to s 134(1) on representative complaints)`
    `s 31 (representative complaints to the commissioner, new ss 146 to 152A)`
    `ss 37 and 38 (representative complaints: withdrawal and extending time, ss 170(6) and 172(2))`
    `ss 46 and 47 (representative complaints in the tribunal, s 193(4) and (5), new ss 194 to 203A)`
    `s 47A (burden of proof, new ss 204 and 205)`
    `s 48 (tribunal orders and costs, s 209)`
    `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 282 and 285 (transitional definitions; existing representative complaints)`
    `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 283, 284, 285A, 286 and 287 (the other transitional provisions)`
    `s 52(2) so far as it inserts the definitions class member and registered employee organisation`
    `s 52(3) (definition complainant)`
    `s 7 (new and renamed attributes, s 7)`
    `s 7A (combined attributes, s 8(2))`
    `s 7B (new meanings of direct and indirect discrimination, ss 10, 11 and 11A)`
    `s 18 (harassment on the basis of sex, chapter 3 part 3)`
    `s 21 (vilification on more grounds, chapter 4 part 4)`
    `s 22 (work environment hostile on the basis of sex, chapter 4 part 5)`
    `s 25 (positive duty, chapter 5C)`
    `s 28(2) to (6) (who may act as my agent, s 134(2), and the other changes to s 134)`
    `s 29 (the 2-year complaint period, s 138)`
    `s 30 (deferring out-of-time contraventions, s 141A)`
    `s 39 (investigations and compliance, chapter 7 part 1A)`
    `s 44 (time limit on referred complaints, s 175)`
    `s 52 other than the parts commencing on 1 December 2024 (the other dictionary changes)`
    `the other amendments in part 2 (ss 4 to 6, 8 to 17, 19, 20, 23, 24, 26, 27, 32 to 36, 40 to 43, 45, 49 and 50)`
    `schedule 1 (other amendments of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991)`
    `part 3 (Corrective Services Act 2006)`
    `ss 56 to 59 (Criminal Code vilification offences)`
    `part 4 heading, s 55 and s 59A (other Criminal Code amendments)`
    `part 6 (Human Rights Act 2019)`
    `parts 5, 6A, 7, 8, 9, 9A and 10 (courts, judges and sentencing)`
    `part 11 and schedule 2 (amendments for the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth))`

DECLARE `When s 2 commences it` IS ONE OF
    `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    `immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources`
    `s 2 does not name it: its commencement is left to the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited`

-- s 2 as passed. s 2(2)(a) "the provisions of part 2 that are not in force on 30 June 2025" is everything in part 2
-- outside s 2(1).
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act`
GIVETH A `When s 2 commences it`
`s 2 -- when it commences` `the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `part 2 heading and s 3 (Act amended)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 28(1) (note to s 134(1) on representative complaints)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 31 (representative complaints to the commissioner, new ss 146 to 152A)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `ss 37 and 38 (representative complaints: withdrawal and extending time, ss 170(6) and 172(2))` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `ss 46 and 47 (representative complaints in the tribunal, s 193(4) and (5), new ss 194 to 203A)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 47A (burden of proof, new ss 204 and 205)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 48 (tribunal orders and costs, s 209)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 282 and 285 (transitional definitions; existing representative complaints)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 52(2) so far as it inserts the definitions class member and registered employee organisation` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 52(3) (definition complainant)` THEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
    WHEN `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 283, 284, 285A, 286 and 287 (the other transitional provisions)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 7 (new and renamed attributes, s 7)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 7A (combined attributes, s 8(2))` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 7B (new meanings of direct and indirect discrimination, ss 10, 11 and 11A)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 18 (harassment on the basis of sex, chapter 3 part 3)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 21 (vilification on more grounds, chapter 4 part 4)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 22 (work environment hostile on the basis of sex, chapter 4 part 5)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 25 (positive duty, chapter 5C)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 28(2) to (6) (who may act as my agent, s 134(2), and the other changes to s 134)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 29 (the 2-year complaint period, s 138)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 30 (deferring out-of-time contraventions, s 141A)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 39 (investigations and compliance, chapter 7 part 1A)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 44 (time limit on referred complaints, s 175)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `s 52 other than the parts commencing on 1 December 2024 (the other dictionary changes)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `the other amendments in part 2 (ss 4 to 6, 8 to 17, 19, 20, 23, 24, 26, 27, 32 to 36, 40 to 43, 45, 49 and 50)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `schedule 1 (other amendments of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `part 3 (Corrective Services Act 2006)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `ss 56 to 59 (Criminal Code vilification offences)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `part 6 (Human Rights Act 2019)` THEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
    WHEN `part 11 and schedule 2 (amendments for the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth))` THEN `immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources`
    OTHERWISE `s 2 does not name it: its commencement is left to the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited`

`1 December 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 12 2024
`1 July 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2025

-- Had the provision commenced on a day, under s 2 as passed? "commence on" a fixed day: before it, JUST FALSE (a period
-- the text fixes); on or after it, JUST TRUE. NOTHING where s 2 gives no day the deposited sources can supply.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act`
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 -- commenced by` `the provision` `the day asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2 -- when it commences` `the provision`
    WHEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))` THEN JUST (NOT (`the day` `the day asked` `is before` `1 December 2024`))
    WHEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))` THEN JUST (NOT (`the day` `the day asked` `is before` `1 July 2025`))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- What the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 deposited beside this Act (act-1991-085, the version in force from 19 May 2025,
-- current on 6 November 2026) shows. Read by hand from that text: for example s 146(2) (registered employee
-- organisations), s 170(6), s 172(2), s 193(4) and (5), ss 194 to 203A, new ss 204 and 205, s 209(5) and (6), ss 282
-- and 285 and the two definitions are there; s 7 still lists "sexuality" and "family responsibilities", ss 10 and 11
-- keep "less favourably" and the proportion test, s 138 keeps "1 year", s 175 keeps "more than 1 year", s 134 has no
-- subsection on industrial agents, chapter 4 part 4 is still "Racial and religious vilification", there is no chapter
-- 3 part 3, s 124E, chapter 5C or chapter 7 part 1A, schedule 1's "unfavourably" wording is unchanged in 14 places and
-- s 131D still reads "204 and 205"; s 285AA stands where ss 283, 284, 285A, 286 and 287 would be.
DECLARE `What the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 shows` IS ONE OF
    `the change is there`
    `the change is not there`
    `nothing to show: the provision makes no change to the text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`
    `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act`
GIVETH A `What the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 shows`
`what the 1991 Act shows of` `the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `ss 1 and 2 (short title and commencement)` THEN `nothing to show: the provision makes no change to the text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`
    WHEN `part 2 heading and s 3 (Act amended)` THEN `nothing to show: the provision makes no change to the text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`
    WHEN `s 28(1) (note to s 134(1) on representative complaints)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `s 31 (representative complaints to the commissioner, new ss 146 to 152A)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `ss 37 and 38 (representative complaints: withdrawal and extending time, ss 170(6) and 172(2))` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `ss 46 and 47 (representative complaints in the tribunal, s 193(4) and (5), new ss 194 to 203A)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `s 47A (burden of proof, new ss 204 and 205)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `s 48 (tribunal orders and costs, s 209)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 282 and 285 (transitional definitions; existing representative complaints)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `s 52(2) so far as it inserts the definitions class member and registered employee organisation` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `s 52(3) (definition complainant)` THEN `the change is there`
    WHEN `part 3 (Corrective Services Act 2006)` THEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`
    WHEN `ss 56 to 59 (Criminal Code vilification offences)` THEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`
    WHEN `part 4 heading, s 55 and s 59A (other Criminal Code amendments)` THEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`
    WHEN `part 6 (Human Rights Act 2019)` THEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`
    WHEN `parts 5, 6A, 7, 8, 9, 9A and 10 (courts, judges and sentencing)` THEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`
    WHEN `part 11 and schedule 2 (amendments for the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth))` THEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here`
    OTHERWISE `the change is not there`

DECLARE `Commencement status` IS ONE OF
    `commenced on 1 December 2024 under s 2(1), and the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 contains it`
    `commenced on 1 December 2024 under s 2(1); it changes no text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`
    `due on 1 July 2025 under s 2(2) as passed, but the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 does not contain it: later legislation, not deposited here, has deferred or changed its commencement`
    `due on 1 July 2025 under s 2(2) as passed; it amends another Act, not checked here`
    `commences immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources`
    `not named in s 2: its commencement is left to the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited`
    `the deposited texts disagree: check the Queensland legislation register`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the amending Act`
GIVETH A `Commencement status`
`the commencement status of` `the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2 -- when it commences` `the provision`
    WHEN `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))` THEN
        CONSIDER `what the 1991 Act shows of` `the provision`
        WHEN `the change is there` THEN `commenced on 1 December 2024 under s 2(1), and the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 contains it`
        WHEN `nothing to show: the provision makes no change to the text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991` THEN `commenced on 1 December 2024 under s 2(1); it changes no text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`
        OTHERWISE `the deposited texts disagree: check the Queensland legislation register`
    WHEN `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))` THEN
        CONSIDER `what the 1991 Act shows of` `the provision`
        WHEN `the change is not there` THEN `due on 1 July 2025 under s 2(2) as passed, but the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 does not contain it: later legislation, not deposited here, has deferred or changed its commencement`
        WHEN `not checked: it amends another Act, which is not checked here` THEN `due on 1 July 2025 under s 2(2) as passed; it amends another Act, not checked here`
        OTHERWISE `the deposited texts disagree: check the Queensland legislation register`
    WHEN `immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources` THEN `commences immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources`
    OTHERWISE `not named in s 2: its commencement is left to the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited`

-- ===================================================================================================================
-- The 1 July 2025 group, as the claimant's questions take it: whether it has commenced, and on what day, are asked
-- (finding 1). The group is treated as commencing together, as s 2(2) commences it (fork F3).
-- ===================================================================================================================

GIVEN `the July 2025 changes have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the July 2025 changes are in force on` `the July 2025 changes have commenced` `the day they commenced` `the day asked` IF
        `the July 2025 changes have commenced`
    AND (NOT (`the day` `the day asked` `is before` `the day they commenced`))
